Subject: [PATCH] Collapse to one column with an audit picker; segment the
 Executive Report
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

leak-map-schedule.tsx:
- Removed the two-column master-detail split. With few audits, the
  narrow left rail left a huge empty column while all the real content
  sat on the right — not a good tradeoff for what's actually normal
  usage. Replaced the always-visible timeline rail with a compact
  dropdown picker button placed right next to the search box (same
  week-grouped list and scope filter, now in a floating panel instead
  of its own column).
- Dropped the right column's own "Monthly audit / timestamp" header —
  the picker button already shows exactly which audit is selected, so
  that title was pure duplication. Detail area is now just "Open full
  page" + the embedded view, full width, one column.

simple-markdown.tsx:
- The report's own convention — a "**Sub-head**" line directly followed
  by a bullet list, once per metric — rendered as two loose blocks with
  nothing to tell one metric's review apart from the next. Now detected
  and grouped into one bordered segment per metric, so "Metric-by-Metric
  Review" actually reads as a list of distinct segments instead of one
  continuous, easy-to-scroll-past wall of text.

leak-map-view.tsx:
- Executive Audit Report now sits in its own bordered container with
  real top margin from whatever's above (Data Gaps, etc.), so it reads
  as a distinct destination on the page instead of a continuation of
  the metrics list you could scroll straight past.

